{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Experiment analysis — ",
    {{ project_id | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Generated by command `llmexer analysis init`.\n",
    "\n",
    "| | |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| project | `",
    {{ project_id | tojson }},
    "` |\n",
    "| llmexer version | `",
    {{ package_version | tojson }},
    "` |\n",
    "| generated | `",
    {{ generated_at | tojson }},
    "` |\n",
    "\n",
    "The cells below only configure paths, call functions and show results.\n",
    "Initial evaluation logic lives in `transform.py`, `stats.py` and `plots.py.\n",
    "Feel free to change the notebook for your needs and data.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Folders\n",
    "\n",
    "The next three cells derive these from `PROJECT_DIR` \n",
    "\n",
    "| variable | path |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `DIR_EXPERIMENT` | `<project>/experiment` |\n| `DB_FILE` | `the database to analyse` |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Change them by hand** if your project is laid out differently — point any of\n",
    "these at an absolute path and re-run the cell, the rest of the notebook follows.\n",
    "\n",
    "`DB_FILE` points to the newest `experiment_*.db` when this notebook was created,\n",
    "**no updates** after creation\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# mapping experiment and search folders \n",
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "ANALYSIS_DIR = Path.cwd()\n",
    "PROJECT_DIR = ANALYSIS_DIR.parent\n",
    "\n",
    "DIR_EXPERIMENT = PROJECT_DIR / 'experiment'\n",
    "PROJECT_ID = ",
    {{ project_id | tojson | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "# `transform`, `stats` and `plots` are the copies sitting next to this notebook\n",
    "if str(ANALYSIS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, str(ANALYSIS_DIR))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# imports of pre-designed methods/functions for analysis\n",
    "%matplotlib inline\n",
    "%load_ext autoreload\n",
    "%autoreload 2\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from plots import (\n",
    "    plot_answers_by_model,\n",
    "    plot_failures_by_model,\n",
    "    plot_flattened_values,\n",
    "    plot_response_time_by_model,\n",
    "    plot_responses_by_model,\n",
    "    plot_tokens_by_model,\n",
    "    setup_style,\n",
    ")\n",
    "from stats import (\n",
    "    answers_by_model,\n",
    "    failed_calls,\n",
    "    response_time_stats,\n",
    "    summary,\n",
    "    token_stats,\n",
    "    total_requests,\n",
    "    total_responses,\n",
    "    value_counts,\n",
    "    value_counts_summary,\n",
    ")\n",
    "from transform import (\n",
    "    export_as_csv,\n",
    "    flatten_llm_response,\n",
    "    flattened_only,\n",
    "    load_experiment_db,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "setup_style()\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.max_colwidth', 120)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# database to analyse \n",
    "DB_FILE = ",
    {{ db_file | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'project      : {PROJECT_ID}')\n",
    "print(f'analysis dir : {ANALYSIS_DIR}')\n",
    "print(f'database     : {DB_FILE}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load the experiment\n",
    "\n",
    "The newest `experiment_*.db` is used; set `DB_PATH` by hand to pick another.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "DB_PATH = DIR_EXPERIMENT / DB_FILE if DB_FILE else None\n",
    "df = load_experiment_db(DB_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'database : {DB_PATH}')\n",
    "print(f'rows     : {total_requests(df)}')\n",
    "df.head()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Flatten the model answers\n",
    "\n",
    "Each `response_text` is parsed as JSON and expanded into columns. Malformed\n",
    "answers keep their row and are reported in `flatten_error`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_flat = flatten_llm_response(df)\n",
    "\n",
    "_bad = df_flat['flatten_error'].ne('')\n",
    "print(f'rows            : {len(df_flat)}')\n",
    "print(f'unparsed answers: {int(_bad.sum())}')\n",
    "df_flat.loc[_bad, ['code', 'flatten_error']].head()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### What to do with the flattened values\n",
    "\n",
    "`df_flat` now carries one column per key the models returned in `response_text`,\n",
    "so the answers can be analysed as data rather than read one by one. A few\n",
    "starting points — adapt the column names to whatever your prompt asks for:\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "# which columns did the answers actually produce?\n",
    "df_flat.columns.difference(df.columns)\n",
    "\n",
    "# how did one answer field come out overall?\n",
    "df_flat['<field>'].value_counts()\n",
    "\n",
    "# do the models agree? one row per model, one column per answer\n",
    "answers_by_model(df_flat, '<field>')\n",
    "\n",
    "# the same input judged by every model, side by side\n",
    "df_flat.pivot_table(index='original_data', columns='model_name',\n",
    "                    values='<field>', aggfunc='first')\n",
    "\n",
    "# where the models disagreed on the same combination\n",
    "df_flat.groupby('code')['<field>'].nunique().pipe(lambda s: s[s > 1])\n",
    "\n",
    "# answers that were not valid JSON — usually a prompt that needs to insist on it\n",
    "df_flat.loc[df_flat['flatten_error'].ne(''), ['code', 'response_text']]\n",
    "```\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Export the answers as CSV\n",
    "\n",
    "The values parsed out of `response_text`, led by `code`, `model_name`,\n",
    "`provider_name` and `profile_name` — enough to tell whose answer each row is,\n",
    "and exactly what the crosstab below groups on. The prompt and the raw payload\n",
    "stay in `df_flat`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "CSV_NAME = f'{Path(DB_FILE).stem}_flattened.csv' if DB_FILE else 'experiment_flattened.csv'\n",
    "answers = flattened_only(df_flat)\n",
    "CSV_PATH = export_as_csv(answers, ANALYSIS_DIR / CSV_NAME)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'written: {CSV_PATH}')\n",
    "answers.head()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## What did the models answer?\n",
    "\n",
    "One row per column parsed out of `response_text`: how many answers carried it,\n",
    "how many distinct values it took, and what kind of answer it is — `boolean`\n",
    "(yes/no, true/false, 1/0), `countable` (whole numbers over a small range, such\n",
    "as a 1-5 rating), `categorical` (a small closed set of labels), or `text` /\n",
    "`nested` / `empty` where a bar chart would say nothing.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "value_summary = value_counts_summary(answers)\n",
    "value_summary\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Counts for a single answer column — change the column name to look at another:\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "VALUE_COLUMN = value_summary.loc[value_summary['plottable'], 'column'].iloc[0] if value_summary['plottable'].any() else None\n",
    "value_counts(answers, VALUE_COLUMN) if VALUE_COLUMN else 'no countable answer columns'\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Every yes/no, countable or small-set answer column, one panel each. Free text\n",
    "and nested answers are left out — they have no small set of values to count.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plot_flattened_values(answers, value_summary);\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Answers by model and provider\n",
    "\n",
    "One row per model, one column per answer value — the same population judged by\n",
    "each model, side by side. A model served by two providers stays two rows, since\n",
    "the two are not the same setup.\n",
    "\n",
    "Rows with no answer — unrun, errored, unparsed, or truncated at `max_tokens` —\n",
    "are left out, so the counts sum to the answers rather than to the generated\n",
    "rows. Change `VALUE_COLUMN` above to look at another answer field.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "answers_by_model(answers, VALUE_COLUMN) if VALUE_COLUMN else 'no countable answer columns'\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plot_answers_by_model(answers, VALUE_COLUMN) if VALUE_COLUMN else print('no countable answer columns');\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Overview\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "summary(df).to_frame()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Responses per model\n",
    "\n",
    "A reply cut short at `max_tokens` is stored as a success by the runner, so it\n",
    "is counted separately as `truncated` and left out of `responses`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "total_responses(df)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Response time per model\n",
    "\n",
    "Finished calls only — unrun rows would drag every mean towards zero.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "response_time_stats(df)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Tokens per model\n",
    "\n",
    "`prompt_tokens` / `completion_tokens` are stored per row by `experiment run`\n",
    "and are left empty where a provider did not report them; `coverage` says how\n",
    "often they were available.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "token_stats(df)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Failed calls\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "failed_calls(df)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Charts\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plot_responses_by_model(df);\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plot_response_time_by_model(df);\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plot_tokens_by_model(df);\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plot_failures_by_model(df);\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
